  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oslo Tropical Forest Forum 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of Oslo Tropical Forest Forum is to strengthen knowledge, action and cooperation between decision-makers, indigenous peoples, civil society and private sector actors who work to stop and reverse tropical deforestation. This year&apos;s conference particularly seeks to build on the international momentum that has arisen in the wake of the global nature agreement and increased global ambitions for forests over the past few years. June 2024 is a good stopping point before the biodiversity convention COP in October 2024r. The conference will help to strengthen the active participation of tropical forest countries in the above-mentioned party meeting, and strengthen the basis for taking into account the interlinkages between nature and climate in  the tropical forest countries&apos; economic development.</narrative>
  </description>
